I don't know the patch in detail, but is it even possible to arrive at a
smoky potion?  I mean, red + yellow = orange makes good sense to me, but
how to solve A + B = smoky?  (Looking at the wiki, I see it's not
possible except by a random outcome, so it doesn't really matter.)

The balance issue seems OK to me.  As long as players aren't start
scumming to get favourable colours (an issue that takes too long to find
out to still call it start scumming), advantages and restrictions of
colour alchemy should keep the balance in a reasonably large number of
games.  A bit like the spellbooks you get and the ones you don't see in
a given game.

